## DEFAULT KERNEL (operator 2026-11-16) -- CURRENT
"release will use 7.4 kernel, no edge and 7.3 will be retired" (26.10 Cygnus PR4,
desktop and server, amd64 and arm64).
- 7.4 is the default AND ONLY kernel line on EVERY arch: amd64
  `7.4.0-rc3-t2-ncz` (package revision `7.4.0-rc3-4`, the rebuild that carries
  7002 and the 7101-7107 AER/DPC series, replacing 9013), arm64 `7.4.0-rc3-sky1-ncz` (package version
  `7.4.0-rc3-sky1-ncz+r303`, staged as r303-7.4.0-rc3-sky1-ncz-20261115).
- Single source of truth: `assets/kernel/default-kernel.json` (both arches). The
  image build gate `build/check-default-kernel.sh` FAILS if the default kernel is
  not 7.4 -- it is a hard fail, never a stderr note (NG2-NC-004).
- The 7.4.0-rc3 base is ACCEPTED for this release (RC_DEFAULT_ALLOWED=1) and must
  move to the final 7.4 kernel in a later PATCH release.
- 7.3.x is retired: no default, no rescue, no installer, no previous-kernel
  entry, not in any apt component for the image (RETIRED_KERNELS_*,
  assets/kernel/KERNEL-LIFECYCLE RETIRED, MIN_VERSION=7.4.0-rc3). The rescue
  entry keeps the unchanged mechanism: the SAME 7.4 default kernel with the
  accelerator drivers blacklisted (RESCUE_SAME_KERNEL=1).
- No EDGE channel: it stays retired (EDGE_ENABLED=0). The edge-kernel lane is
  cancelled and unmerged; do not re-add edge assets, pointers or entries.
- Sky1 stays MALI ONLY: CONFIG_DRM_PANTHOR is off in the 7.4 kernel config, no
  panthor module or package is built or installed, and mali_kbase plus the Mali
  userspace are required. Enforced by `build/test-mali-only-image.sh` and
  `build/test-default-kernel-gate.sh`.
- Enforced by `build/check-default-kernel.sh` (hard 7.4 policy line above) +
  `build/verify-kernel-default-policy.sh` + `build/check-kernel-lifecycle.py`.
